00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:58.350
existing platforms talk to each other. Think of it like the internet.

196
00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:06.340
We didn't build one website that everyone has to use. We built H.T.T.P., the protocol that lets all websites connect.

197
00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:14.660
Same idea. How your decentralized F.D.A. gets funded: An implementation of this framework is one of many campaigns competing

198
00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:18.620
for funding from the one percent Treaty Fund via Wishocracy.

199
00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:25.920
It has no independent budget authority. If a particular implementation gets captured or fails to deliver, the community

200
00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:31.000
can fund alternative implementations instead. This prevents the "new F.D.A."

201
00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:39.280
problem. The Players Already in the Game. Multiple companies have already built decentralized clinical trial platforms.

